{"format":1,"seq":161,"writes":[{"type":"entry","value":{"model":[{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is a big scope, so I'm thinking about splitting it into separate PRs: one covering npm/git additions and renderers, and another for sandbox type changes like workspace.edit widening and atob/btoa declarations, since those are independent enough to ship separately.\n\nBut both touch the generated global-contract.d.ts file, which could cause merge conflicts since the preamble gets regenerated — though that's fixable with a regen. I'm leaning toward one combined src PR for globals and types, plus a separate PR for project functions in .pi/functions, but that second PR could want to use the new git globals internally, creating a dependency; I'm weighing whether to stack it on the first PR's branch versus keeping it independent and using something like shell.execFile as an internal workaround, even though the guidance favors typed git methods.\n\nNow I'm redefining the waits API: timeouts should never throw regardless of the raise flag, instead returning an outcome of \"pending\" with a hint to retry, while raise still governs failures. I'm sketching the shared result shape for waitForRun — completed runs get outcome \"passed\"/\"failed\" plus attempt, status, conclusion, url, and jobs, while timeouts get outcome \"pending\" with elapsed time, attempts, timeout info, and a hint — and reconsidering how the old \"timed_out\" status field should map into this new contract.\n\nFor waitForCommit I'm having it propagate the run's outcome and conclusion alongside the match and run, while discovery failures (no run found before the deadline) still throw since that's a distinct synchronization issue, not a pending timeout. I'm also drafting the hint text that tells callers exactly how to re-invoke waitForRun to keep waiting.\n\nNow I'm updating the \"raise\" semantics docs to clarify that a timeout always returns outcome \"pending\" regardless of raise, and noting the existing tests (workflow-ci.test.ts, workflow-pr-checks.test.ts) plus the pit-delivery skill docs that reference the old \"call again\" wording will need corresponding updates. I'm also starting to sketch out delivery.openPullRequest's input shape and its steps for switching branches and committing with push enabled.\n\nI need to check delivery.commit's push semantics around setting the upstream, then continue the flow through gh.prCreate and defining the return shape with branch, commit sha, and url. I also want to work out pr.merge's logic—calling gh.prMerge, optionally syncing by switching to the base branch and fast-forward pulling—and then check the existing test helpers and README/skill docs to make sure all these new functions get properly documented and tested.\n\n","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_bdrk_0124yrrZXCvSQA6XGDnJbVfB","name":"typescript","arguments":{"code":"// @pit: {\"label\": \"Read delivery.commit, workflow test helper, CI workflow tests\"}\nasync ({ workspace: { batch, glob } }) => {\n  const r = await batch([\n    { kind: \"read\", file: \".pi/functions/delivery/commit.ts\", options: { format: \"raw\" } },\n    { kind: \"read\", file: \"test/helpers/workflow-function.ts\", options: { format: \"raw\" } },\n    { kind: \"read\", file: \"test/functions/workflow-ci.test.ts\", options: { format: \"raw\" } },\n    { kind: \"read\", file: \".pi/functions/README.md\", options: { format: \"raw\" } },\n  ]);\n  const g = await glob([\"test/functions/workflow-*.test.ts\"]);\n  return { files: r.results.map((x: any) => x.value?.content ?? x), g: g.entries };\n}"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"nvidia","model":"aws/anthropic/bedrock-claude-opus-5-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":2108,"cacheRead":59587,"cacheWrite":7668,"totalTokens":69365,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0,"totalFromProvider":false},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":1775},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1794